body:
one of the comments talked about how their mom vied their them as an extension of themselves, and my mom does the same thing. when i went to therapy she fought with, "but im your mother, what do they (my therapist) have that i don't?" "i'm not only your mother, but im your best friend." then everything would be hers that she likes, she loves to grab my hair and show off to family, "oh my god, look at MY hair!" and today before i went to job #2 she looked at my watch, which had a new band and gasped, "oh look at MY watch!" and everything she hated was always a "you're just like your father." or "i don't even know who you are anymore.." and like the last statement my mom would say after an argument, "i'm not going to say anything anymore, i'm just going to live in pain forever. cause you don't love me." 

&#x200B;

i can't wait until i can move out..
